namespace trion.propositional:
    primitive query example
    primitive artifact identifier, query document identifier, target formula reference

    source PROP-QUERY-EXAMPLES:
        title "Worked queries and expected results"
        locator "urn:trion:propositional:query-examples:1"
        kind citation
        quote CASES """
Premises P implies Q and P entail Q, with consistent premises.
Premises P implies Q and Q do not entail P. P=false and Q=true is a counterexample.
Premises P and not P entail Q vacuously.
With no declarations and no premises, the empty valuation refutes entailment of false.
"""

    section "A query fixes its document and premises":
        cite FOUNDATION
        The kind of a query is satisfiability or entailment.
        A query identifies one document.
        A query uses every premise of the document of the query.
        A satisfiability query has no target formula.
        An entailment query has exactly one target formula.

        [Q-BINDING]
        If the query document identifier differs from the artifact identifier, then the propositional core shall reject the query.
        The propositional core shall check every reference of a target formula.

        [Q-MODEL]
        A valuation is a premise model exactly when every premise is true.

        [Q-SAT]
        Premises are satisfiable exactly when a premise model exists.

        [Q-UNSAT]
        Premises are unsatisfiable exactly when no premise model exists.

        [Q-COUNTEREXAMPLE]
        A valuation is a counterexample exactly when the valuation is a premise model and the target is false.

        [Q-ENTAILS]
        A target follows exactly when no counterexample exists.

        [Q-INCONSISTENT]
        Contradictory premises have no premise model.
        Each target follows from contradictory premises.

        [Q-EMPTY]
        Every valuation satisfies the empty premise set.

        [Q-EXAMPLES]
        The propositional checker shall check the query examples.
            cite PROP-QUERY-EXAMPLES#CASES

        [Q-OPEN]
        Non-entailment differs from entailment of the negation.
